<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-sequences" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Sequences </title>

    <definition>
      <statement>
        <p>Informally, a <term>sequence</term> (of real numbers) is an infinite list of real numbers.</p>
        <p>Formally, a sequence is a function from the natural numbers to 
        the real numbers <m>a: \N \rightarrow \R</m>. Rather than writing <m>a(n)</m>,
        we typically use <m>a_n</m> to refer to the nth term of the sequence,
        and write <m>\{a_n\}_{n=1}^\infty</m> to represent the whole sequence.
        </p>
      </statement>
    </definition>

    <example>
      <p>
        <m>\{0.9,0.99,0.999,0.9999,0.99999,\ldots\}</m> is a sequence.
        It represents the function from <m>\N</m> to <m>\R</m> given by
        <md>n \rightarrow 1-\frac{1}{10^{n}}.</md>
        We could also represent this sequence as <m>\{1-\frac{1}{10^{n}}\} _{n=1} ^\infty</m>.
      </p>
    </example>

    <activity>
      <introduction>
        <p>
          Write the first 5 terms of each of these sequences
        </p>
      </introduction>
      <task>
        <statement>
          <m>\{\frac{1}{n}\}_{n=1} ^\infty</m>
        </statement>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement>
          <m>\{2^n\}_{n=1} ^\infty</m>
        </statement>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement>
          <m>\{\frac{n-1}{n}\}_{n=1} ^\infty</m>
        </statement>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement>
          <m>\{(-1)^n\}_{n=1} ^\infty</m>
        </statement>
      </task>
      <task>
        <statement>
          <p>
            How would you describe each of these sequences, particularly as <m>n</m> becomes large?
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>
    </activity>


</section>